TASK FEAT77
	TITLE "Locate every validation issue in a way a repair can act on"
	STATUS draft
	SPEC "every issue the validator reports names the section it concerns, and the ones bearing on"
		+ "one entry name that entry in a single index space, whichever code they carry"
	SPEC "a float serialization issue names the section and the entry it concerns, as the issues of"
		+ "a section schema do with their section location and their entry index"
	SPEC "a save designating no host or more than one reaches its presenter through an outcome"
		+ "naming the player entries designated host, where today that outcome carries their count"
		+ "only"
	SPEC "the sentences the command line and the save manager display for an invalid save are"
		+ "unchanged"
	WAVE @WAVE.7
	RATIONALE "A fix the user ticks has to be applied to one entry of one section, and today an"
		+ "issue cannot say which. The codes that carry an entryIndex do not count in the same"
		+ "space: the unreadable line carries its rank among the lines of the section, each schema"
		+ "violation its rank among the readable entries alone, so one unreadable line above a"
		+ "violation shifts every index below it and a repair would rewrite the wrong entry. Since"
		+ "wave 14 an issue carries a code and its data, no sentence: the issues of a section"
		+ "schema carry their section, their entry and the path of their field, and the float"
		+ "serialization issue its field and its value but no section nor entry, because it scans"
		+ "the raw text. A save designating no host or more than one is no longer an issue: it"
		+ "reaches its presenter through an outcome of its own carrying the host count, which names"
		+ "no player entry. Nothing here changes what the validator accepts or refuses, so the"
		+ "single source of warnings stays one source and the four flows keep their verdict; only"
		+ "the shape of an issue grows. This is the precondition of the fix catalogue and of"
		+ "everything the rest of the wave applies"
		REF @COMMAND.ValidateSave
		REF @DECISION.ValidationIsTheSingleSourceOfWarnings
		REF @RULE.ASectionLineIsOneJsonEntry
		REF @RULE.FloatFieldsCarryADotZeroSuffixInFlatRecords
		REF @RULE.ASaveDesignatesExactlyOneHostPlayer
		REF @SECTION.Players
		REF @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	SOURCE "User ruling of 2026-09-21 on pull request #108: its wave 7 tasks are rejected; the"
		+ "repair rests on the existing validator, detects the defects of the save, presents a"
		+ "table of fixes to tick and writes a new save file on confirmation"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST
	SOURCE "Read on 2026-09-21 on the default branch: the unreadable line carries the rank of the"
		+ "line in its section and the schema violation the rank of the entry among the readable"
		+ "ones, the field name sits inside the detail sentence as the instance path of the schema"
		+ "error, and the float serialization and unique host issues carry neither section nor"
		+ "entry"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST
		REF @PACKAGE.core_mapping

TASK FEAT78
	TITLE "Propose the fixes that repair a save the validator rejects"
	STATUS draft
	SPEC "a save the validator rejects yields a plan listing, for each proposed fix, the issues it"
		+ "resolves, what the save carries before and what it will carry after, whether the fix"
		+ "discards data, and whether it can be left out or comes with any rewritten file"
	SPEC "a defect for which no fix is known appears in the plan as not repairable automatically,"
		+ "and never disappears from it"
	SPEC "a save the validator accepts yields a plan proposing no fix"
	SPEC "a save whose section count is unsupported yields a plan saying so and saying that no"
		+ "other defect could be looked for"
	AFTER @TASK.FEAT77
	WAVE @WAVE.7
	RATIONALE "The table the user confirms is this plan, so the plan is built before any UI exists"
		+ "and is tested without one. Building it needs the sections of a save the validator"
		+ "rejects, which no use case exposes today: the use cases that load and merge a save"
		+ "return before reading its sections when validation fails, while SaveSectionsReaderPort"
		+ "never refuses a save: a line it cannot parse and an entry it cannot decode into the"
		+ "business types of the domain come back as unreadable lines, every other entry decoded."
		+ "The plan therefore reads the issues from the validator, the single source, the host"
		+ "designation from the unique host rule of the domain, no longer an issue of the validator"
		+ "since wave 14, and the sections through that reader port, and pairs them; it invents no"
		+ "detection of its own. Two defects need no fix code at all, the unreadable line and the"
		+ "undecodable entry being already dropped by the reader and the float suffix being already"
		+ "written back by the serializer, which is why the plan is worth its own task before"
		+ "anything is applied. A defect with no known fix stays visible: a repair that hides what"
		+ "it cannot mend is worse than one that mends nothing"
		REF @COMMAND.ValidateSave
		REF @DECISION.ValidationIsTheSingleSourceOfWarnings
		REF @RULE.ASaveHasElevenSectionsTheLastReservedAndEmpty
		REF @RULE.FloatFieldsCarryADotZeroSuffixInFlatRecords
		REF @RULE.ASaveDesignatesExactlyOneHostPlayer
		REF @TASK.FEAT77
		REF @PACKAGE.core_mapping
		REF @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	SOURCE "User ruling of 2026-09-21 on pull request #108: the defects of the save are detected by"
		+ "the existing validator and presented as a table of the fixes to apply, the user ideally"
		+ "ticking which ones"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST
	SOURCE "Read on 2026-09-21 on the default branch: the parser records an unreadable line and"
		+ "continues, the display and merge use cases call it only after a valid verdict, and the"
		+ "entry serializer writes the dot zero suffix back for the twelve float fields the check"
		+ "scans"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST
		REF @PACKAGE.core_mapping

TASK FEAT79
	TITLE "Write a new save file applying the fixes the caller selected"
	STATUS draft
	SPEC "applying a selection of fixes produces new save content, leaves the content it was given"
		+ "untouched, and reports the validation of the result"
	SPEC "the fixes the rewrite itself carries are applied whatever the selection, and the result"
		+ "lists them"
	SPEC "the result names the issues that remain and the selected fixes that could not be applied,"
		+ "each with its reason"
	SPEC "a player identifier beyond the range of a double comes out of the repair as the same"
		+ "decimal text it went in with"
	SPEC "a save carrying the legacy twelve part format comes out in the eleven section format, and"
		+ "the result says that the terrain layers are not carried over"
	AFTER @TASK.FEAT78
	WAVE @WAVE.7
	RATIONALE "This is where the repair writes. The whole result is produced by parsing the"
		+ "rejected save through SaveSectionsParserPort as the merge does, applying the selected"
		+ "fixes to the sections decoded into the business types of the domain and serializing them"
		+ "again through SaveSectionsSerializerPort, so the two defects the round trip already"
		+ "mends cost no fix code and the third, several host players, is a single assignment on"
		+ "the players section. Serializing is what makes the repair risky rather than the fixes:"
		+ "an entry the decoding cannot read comes back from that port as an unreadable line and"
		+ "never reaches the entry serializer, which refuses a nested value, and whether every"
		+ "nested field is such an entry is measured at refinement, a save the serializer still"
		+ "refuses coming back as a named failure instead of a thrown error; the identifier of a"
		+ "player is written as its exact decimal text and must not be parsed into a number on the"
		+ "way through; and the serializer writes ten sections, so a legacy save is converted"
		+ "whether or not the user asked. The result is validated again before it is handed back,"
		+ "exactly as the merge validates its own output, and what remains is reported rather than"
		+ "swallowed"
		REF @DECISION.ValidationIsTheSingleSourceOfWarnings
		REF @RULE.APlayerIdentifierIsCarriedAsExactDecimalText
		REF @RULE.FloatFieldsCarryADotZeroSuffixInFlatRecords
		REF @RULE.ASaveHasElevenSectionsTheLastReservedAndEmpty
		REF @RULE.APlayerEntryCarriesCameraViewAndItsLifetimeTotals
		REF @SECTION.Players
		REF @SECTION.Reserved
		REF @TASK.FEAT78
		REF @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	SOURCE "User ruling of 2026-09-21 on pull request #108: on confirmation a new save file is"
		+ "created carrying the corrections, the file loaded being never overwritten"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST
	SOURCE "Read on 2026-09-21 on the default branch: the merge use case validates the content it"
		+ "has just serialized before presenting it, the entry serializer throws on a nested field,"
		+ "and the round trip of an int64 player identifier is covered by the serializer"
		+ "specification"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST
		REF @PACKAGE.core_mapping

TASK FEAT80
	TITLE "Repair a rejected save from the save manager"
	STATUS draft
	SPEC "loading a save the validator rejects shows, besides its errors, the defects grouped by"
		+ "kind with the fix proposed for each; a fix that can be left out carries a box to tick,"
		+ "and a fix any rewritten file carries is shown as always applied, with what it discards"
	SPEC "a defect for which no fix is proposed is shown as such, with the entry it concerns and no"
		+ "box"
	SPEC "confirming downloads a new file under a name distinct from the loaded one, and shows what"
		+ "the validator still reports about it"
	SPEC "a save whose section count is unsupported shows the one defect it produces and no repair"
		+ "to confirm"
	AFTER @TASK.FEAT79
	AFTER @TASK.FEAT70
	WAVE @WAVE.7
	RATIONALE "Today a rejected save ends the page: the route shows the list of validation messages"
		+ "and nothing else, and the visualization area stays empty. The repair view takes that"
		+ "dead end and turns it into the table the user acts on, reusing the export path the wave"
		+ "before builds so that the corrected save leaves as a new file and the loaded one is"
		+ "never overwritten. Grouping by kind is what makes the table usable when a defect repeats"
		+ "across hundreds of entries. A fix the rewrite itself carries cannot be left out, the"
		+ "reader having already dropped the unreadable line and the undecodable entry and the"
		+ "serializer writing the float suffix back, so it is shown as always applied with the loss"
		+ "named in its row rather than behind a box that could not be honoured, because a save"
		+ "manager that silently drops entries of a save is the failure this feature exists to"
		+ "avoid. A call that does not complete keeps the one failure idiom of the package,"
		+ "distinct from what the validator reports"
		REF @DECISION.UiSaveManagerHasOneUiErrorIdiom
		REF @DECISION.ValidationIsTheSingleSourceOfWarnings
		REF @DECISION.AGuardRefusesLocatorsTheScreenDoesNotShow
		REF @TASK.FEAT79
		REF @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager
		REF @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	SOURCE "User ruling of 2026-09-21 on pull request #108: the defects are presented as a table of"
		+ "the fixes to apply, ideally with a box per fix, and confirming creates a new corrected"
		+ "save file"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST
	SOURCE "Read on 2026-09-21 on the default branch: the display route renders the validation"
		+ "messages and the visualization area is shown only when the save carries no error, and"
		+ "the merge result is the only place that turns serialized content into a downloadable"
		+ "file"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST
		REF @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager

