TASK FEAT190
	TITLE "Show the toxicity gauge on the player card"
	STATUS draft
	DESC "stays draft until DOCS193 reports the toxic time of every toxic area: one time shared by"
		+ "every area is the maximum of the gauge; differing times reopen the refinement, the save"
		+ "not carrying the area a player stands in"
		REF @TASK.DOCS193
	SPEC "a player card whose playerGaugeToxic is above 0 shows a fourth flat gauge for toxicity,"
		+ "filled by percentage of its maximum like the three vital gauges, the percentage next to"
		+ "the label and the value over its maximum under the gauge; a card at 0 shows none, as the"
		+ "game hides its meter"
	SPEC "the toxicity gauge shows the protection left, its maximum less playerGaugeToxic, as the"
		+ "meter of the game does: full at no exposure, empty once playerGaugeToxic reaches the"
		+ "maximum, where the game damages the player"
	SPEC "the toxicity maximum is the toxic time DOCS193 reads, from a value table of a data-"
		+ "package, by an infrastructure adapter behind an application port, no equipment changing"
		+ "it; the use case hands value, maximum and percentage to the presenter as primitives of"
		+ "its application response"
		REF @TASK.DOCS193
	SPEC "a RULE states that playerGaugeToxic is the exposure a player has accumulated in a toxic"
		+ "area, 0 for none, capped at the toxic time of that area, attested by the tests of the"
		+ "gauge"
	SPEC "the specs of cli-merge and cli-validate pass unchanged"
	AFTER @TASK.FEAT144
	AFTER @TASK.DOCS193
	RATIONALE "The save carries the toxicity of each player as playerGaugeToxic, without its"
		+ "maximum. The game accumulates it while the player stands in a toxic area that is not"
		+ "fully cleaned, at a rate a Toxins Filter in the equipment slows, caps it at the toxic"
		+ "time of that area and damages the player there, then drains it outside; its meter shows"
		+ "the maximum less that value and hides at 0. The maximum is a value of each area, set in"
		+ "the scene, and the save does not say which area a player stands in: the gauge can be"
		+ "drawn only if every area shares one time. The 4.9999995 of the private reference save"
		+ "Standard-5-toxic.json is then a player at the cap of an area whose time is 5, an empty"
		+ "meter"
		REF @SECTION.Players
		REF @DECISION.APlayerGaugeIsMeasuredAgainstTheMaximumItsEquipmentGives
		REF @TASK.DOCS193
		REF @PROJECT.DNC
	SOURCE "Split from FEAT144 in the review of pull request 263"
